Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is “financial point of view” the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.2. Change in Company Recommendation. <omitted> (c) Notwithstanding anything in this Agreement to the contrary, the Company Board may, at any time prior to obtaining the Company Stockholder Approval, make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change if: (i) the Company Board, after consultation with its outside legal counsel, determines in good faith that a failure to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change would be inconsistent with its fiduciary duties under applicable Law, and (ii) the Company has provided Parent with at least three business days' prior written notice of its intention to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change, including a summary of the reasons for such change. During this notice period, the Company shall, and shall cause its legal advisors to, negotiate with Parent in good faith (to the extent Parent desires to negotiate) to make such adjustments to the terms and conditions of this Agreement so that a Company Adverse Recommendation Change is no longer necessary. If the Company receives a new Acquisition Proposal during this period, it shall notify Parent of the material terms and conditions of such proposal, and any changes to the financial terms or other material amendments to such proposal shall require a new notice to Parent and a new three business day period. (Pages 83-84)
